Array in Java
What is an Array?

An array is a fixed-size data structure.

It stores elements of the same data type.

Once created, its size cannot be changed.

Example
int[] numbers = new int[5];

Ways to Initialize an Array
1️⃣ Declaration + Initialization
int[] arr = new int[3];
arr[0] = 10;
arr[1] = 20;
arr[2] = 30;

2️⃣ Declaration + Direct Values
int[] arr = {10, 20, 30};

3️⃣ Using new Keyword with Values
int[] arr = new int[] {10, 20, 30};

Accessing Array Elements
System.out.println(arr[0]); // 10
